  "summary": "DIR-065 COMPLETE. (1) ADAPTIVE PARTITIONER: smartPartitioner.js no longer estimates grid cards as linear text. Added a shared pairGridRows() row-paired estimator that charges each 2-column row Math.max(cardA, cardB) + rowGap, carrying the row height on the row-start card so a row is atomic; added projectCardHeightFor() calibrated to the real .smart-card-item (>=65px floor, 92px ceiling, density-scaled) replacing the old ~36px linear project estimate; routed certifications through the same estimator with certRowHeightFor (>=76px floor) so a taller partner card can no longer be under-counted; and raised the footer clearance to a dynamic, density-scaled FOOTER_SAFETY_CLEARANCE = Math.max(36, 40 * densityScale). smartEngine.css now gives .smart-card-item break-inside:avoid and a matching .smart-page-body buffer. The exact defect profile is fixed: the Babu M '5 projects + 5 certifications' fixture (template-lab/fixtures.js gridDense) previously fast-pathed all 10 cards onto page 1 at 868px vs 878px capacity while the real DOM was 967px (+89px) and crushed the 5th card into the footer; it now partitions to 2 pages with the last cert row on page 2 under an authentic continuation header. (2) DOCX<->PDF PARITY: backend/services/docxExport.js now renders structured 2-column OOXML CARD tables (CARD_FILL F8FAFC, CARD_BORDER E2E8F0, CARD_CELL_MARGINS padding, bold title + meta hierarchy) via new buildProjectCardCell() and buildCertCardCell(); buildProjectsBlock() emits title/url/description cards matching SmartProjects.jsx; buildCertificationsBlock()'s two-column branch replaces borderless bullet cells with real cards matching SmartCertifications.jsx; buildModernSplitDocument() now enables 2-column card mode for certifications. (3) ENVIRONMENT: pure Linux-server-compatible; the new template-lab/census-probe.mjs spawns no OS process, no native console, no winget/cmd/PowerShell; src/cv-templates git diff = 0; XAMPP policy guard 4/4. EVIDENCE: new tests/dir065-adaptive-partitioner-docx-parity.test.mjs 9/9 (incl. FUNCTIONAL: a row is charged the TALLER card (>=95px) not the row-start card; the 5+5 gridDense profile spills onto page 2 with project rows >=65px and cert rows >=76px; DOCX emits F8FAFC fill + E2E8F0 border + equal-width 2-column card tables carrying the 5th project and 5th certification). DIR-064+DIR-065+DIR-063 27/27 (DIR-064 constants updated for the DIR-065 supersede); backend DOCX export+parity 25/25 (the Cv4 no-split-sidebar assertion was refined from the now-ambiguous F8FAFC proxy to the real 34/66 grid-ratio check, since F8FAFC is now also the mandated card fill); product slice 115/115. HEADLESS PLAYWRIGHT DOM CENSUS: template-lab/census-probe.mjs over ALL 55 templates on the gridDense fixture -> every CV renders 2 pages / 10 cards / worstOverlap 0px; 'CENSUS PASS: no grid card overlaps the page footer across 55 template(s)'. Overflow probe (long, 55 templates): 0 clipped elements, probe failures 0. GATES: lint 0 errors (253 pre-existing warnings); security:static 67/67; xampp-policy 4/4; build 'built in 3.52s' (under the 4.0s budget). HONEST LIMITS: the DOM census proves zero card/footer overlap for the gridDense profile and the overflow probe proves zero page-bottom clipping for the long profile, but neither re-runs the exact user's original private resume; the estimator clamps project cards at 92px and cert cards at 88px, so a pathologically long (4+ line) card relies on the CSS break-inside:avoid + page-body buffer as the backstop; sidebar certifications still render as bullets in DOCX (columns:1 path) because the sidebar cell width is not threaded into the builder, so card parity is exact in the main flow but not in the sidebar."
